\left(x^2+1\right)=$(x-2)(x+2)$
Let $f(x)=x^3+a x^2+b x+c ; a, b, c \in\{1,2, \ldots, 10\}f(x)$ is divisible by $x^2+1$ iff $f(i)=0, f(-i)=0\therefore \quad i^3+a i^2+b $i+c=0\begin{array}{rrr}\Rightarrow$ \text{ and } -i-a+b i+c=0 \\ \Rightarrow \text{ and } a=c, b=1\end{array}
and $\quad-i³+a i²-b i+c=0\begin{array}{rr}\Rightarrow \text{ and } i-a-b i+c=0 \\ \Rightarrow \text{ and } a=c, b=1\end{array}
\therefore$ Total number of selection of triplets
$(a, b, c)=(1,1,1),(2,1,2), \ldots,(10,1,10)$
Hence, number of such polynomials $=10$.$

Set $S=\{1,2,3, \ldots, 20\}$ is to be partitioned into four sets of equal size i.e., having $5-5$ numbers.
The number of ways in which it can be done
$\begin{aligned}
& ={ }^{20} C_5 \times{ }^{15} C_5 \times{ }^{10} C_5 \times{ }^5 C_5 \\
& =\frac{20!}{15!\times 5!} \times \frac{15!}{10!\times 5!} \times \frac{10!}{5!\times 5!} \times 1=\frac{(20!)}{(5!)^4}
\end{aligned}$
